notes:EXECUTION DIRECTIVE 2026-07-28: Design the closed rust-v1 and rust-repository-v1 pair from the independently accepted TASK-260728-2spy93 and TASK-260728-1g0z69 contracts. Consume TASK-260729-rhjxtx rework-cycle-1 artifacts as measured but still review-pending evidence; do not turn an unreviewed observation or absent Windows/Linux toolchain into a platform claim. Complete every reserved Rust registry field and acceptance layer: trusted root/executable identity, exact version/target probes and normalization, compatibility family, metadata disposition, Cargo/rustc argv/process graph, source_dir and skill-build.json mapping, artifact identity, cache/receipt/marker effects, and fail-before-compiler diagnostics. Exhaustively decide Cargo.lock/vendor/config/workspaces/features/build.rs/proc-macro/plugin/target/linker/FFI/bindgen/native-lib/network/registry surfaces under portable manager-worker, with package-selected paths/env/toolchains/channels/install/network/trust rejected and no auto-install. Cover local vendored and exact external repository modes, macOS primary, Windows implementation contract without false native qualification, and later Linux qualification rules. Produce decision/reference/vectors or executable probes required by the task, preserve frozen released artifacts, and do not stage/commit/publish/pin; hand off with full deterministic evidence.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-52b118, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-52b118)\nProgress 2026-07-29: host-measured recon complete on macOS 26.5 arm64 / Rust 1.91.0. Decisive result: with SDKROOT pinned and -Clinker=<root>/lib/rustlib/<target>/bin/rust-lld -Clinker-flavor=ld64.lld, a full vendored offline cargo build produced a running Mach-O arm64 executable with ZERO PATH-resolved executables (poisoned-PATH shim probe, 20 names, 0 hits); the red control without those pins resolved xcrun and cc from PATH. Process closure is therefore cargo->rustc->rust-lld, entirely inside the fingerprinted Rust root; the macOS SDK is a data-only second fingerprinted root (261MB, 32345 files, 7448 links). Also measured: cargo metadata does NOT execute build.rs or proc macros (marker-file probe, both absent, exit 0) and reports custom-build/proc-macro target kinds plus links and source, so the pre-compile rejection matrix is decidable in the graph phase; --locked prevents any Cargo.lock write into the frozen snapshot; a package .cargo/config.toml rustc-wrapper DID run a package-selected executable and an ancestor .cargo/config.toml is also discovered, while RUSTC_WRAPPER= in the manager environment neutralised both and a config [env] force=true could not override it; rust-toolchain.toml carrying both path and nightly is fully inert against a directly resolved cargo. rust-version has three host-independent acceptance layers (TOML type, RustVersion grammar, edition floor) plus a separate host gate, each with distinct measured diagnostics. Writing decision 0009 + reference + boundary probe next.\nHANDOFF 2026-07-29: decision 0009 + implementation-ready reference + executable boundary probe, all attached. Two decisive host measurements. (1) Process closure: with SDKROOT and -Clinker=<root>/lib/rustlib/<target>/bin/rust-lld -Clinker-flavor=ld64.lld pinned, both the graph and the compile phase produced ZERO PATH resolutions against 20 logging shims and yielded a running Mach-O arm64 binary depending only on libSystem; the unpinned control resolved xcrun and cc. Closure is cargo->rustc->rust-lld inside the fingerprinted Rust root, with the macOS SDK as a data-only second root, so no sixth toolchain identifier is coined and toolchain_identities stays at one element. (2) cargo metadata executes no build.rs and no proc macro (marker probe, both absent, exit 0) while reporting custom-build/proc-macro/links/source, which is what makes the decision 0008 section 7 pre-compile matrix computable. Also measured: --locked prevents a Cargo.lock write into the frozen snapshot; a package and an ancestor .cargo/config.toml both execute a package-named rustc wrapper, neutralised by an empty RUSTC_WRAPPER but rejected outright anyway; rust-toolchain.toml is inert against direct resolution. One correction to decision 0007: Cargo.toml rust-version moves from compared to classified because it has three measured host-independent acceptance layers (TOML type, grammar, edition floor) plus an excluded host gate, with F empty so P1/P2 collapse to C = Upstream. Probe green exit 0: 19/19 cases, 24 closure checks 0 verdicts, 6/6 controls failing as required, 8/8 structural checks. platforms holds only (macos, arm64); macOS amd64, Windows and Linux are qualification obligations with a stated acceptance test, never claims. Two residual exposures stated not closed: compile-time file inclusion (needs a seventh deferred guarantee in STORY-260728-327soo) and FFI against base-installation libraries. Gates: probe gofmt/vet/build/test 0, probe runs 0, curator build/vet/test/gofmt 0; make check 2 and spec validate.py 1 are expected-red and attributed to other tasks trees, with a clean-tree validate baseline at 0 and a scoped link check over the two authored documents at 0. golangci-lint NOT RUN, not installed on this host. Decision number 0009 reserved; renumbers if Swift or Kotlin lands it first.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-52b118, pid=90707, exit=0)\nREVIEW CYCLE 1 DIRECTIVE: Independently review the Rust pair; do not edit artifacts. Treat accepted decisions 0007/0008 as authoritative and reject silent contract drift. Specifically adjudicate the proposed rust-version disposition change from compared to a seven-class classified boundary; require proof it is a compatible narrowing and complete/exhaustive, not a reserved-wire change. Verify rust-v1 and rust-repository-v1 are closed, exact registry/fingerprint/compatibility/metadata fields are implementation-ready, Cargo.lock/vendor/workspace/features/build.rs/proc-macro/links/config/ancestor config/path dependency/git/registry/network/wrapper/target/linker/SDK/FFI/bindgen/native-library surfaces are exhaustively handled before compile, and cargo metadata itself cannot read/resolve outside admitted roots, mutate the snapshot, execute package code, or use untrusted config/environment. Challenge the multi-root closure and manager-written CARGO_HOME, SDK data-only claim, rust-lld/target stdlib checks, per-operation 918MB hashing cost, local versus repository equivalence, stable diagnostics, and produced-binary signing boundary. Re-run the standalone probe and all six expected-red controls, inspect raw fixtures/argv/env/markers and absence behavior, and distinguish measured macOS arm64 from unqualified Windows/Linux. Expected-red unrelated repository gates are not acceptance evidence; confirm scoped authored artifacts and links. Publish TASK-260728-12pnm1_review-verdict-cycle-1.md with ACCEPTED or exact CHANGES REQUESTED and route accordingly.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-de06b1, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-de06b1)\nREVIEW CYCLE 1 VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED and routed to analysis. Independent replay is green: probe test/vet/build 0, full and controls-only probe 0 with 19/19 cases, P1/P2 true, 24 closure checks, 6/6 required controls, 8/8 structural checks; Curator test/vet 0; resource/worktree documents byte-identical. Four contract blockers remain: curator-rust-toolchain-v1 rejects multiline rustc -vV under its own normalization; the fixed cargo metadata argv lacks --all-features while the contract and vector 19 claim an all-feature union; G6/G7 discover outside-root path dependencies only after Cargo has read/resolved them; and the probe does not exercise the exact manager-written Cargo config, vendored dependency, exact argv, or both source modes, while Windows TOML path serialization is unspecified. Rust-version classified narrowing and macOS closure/platform/signing boundaries otherwise pass review. Full evidence and re-review gate: TASK-260728-12pnm1_review-verdict-cycle-1.md. Reviewer supplied no commit_ack.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-de06b1, pid=21862, exit=0)\nREWORK CYCLE 2 DIRECTIVE (review cycle 1): Resolve exactly the four accepted review blockers in the preserved Rust task worktree; retain every green finding and do not widen platform claims. (1) Make curator-rust-toolchain-v1 independently computable from real multiline rustc -vV. Prefer a closed multiline normalization (CRLF to LF, reject bare CR/NUL/invalid UTF-8, exact terminal-LF rule) inside the existing length framing, or bind one explicitly extracted whole release line; whichever is chosen must update decision/reference/identity example/probe plus positive and line/byte mutation vectors. (2) Keep the deliberate conservative all-feature union and add --all-features to the exact metadata argv; prove every package unit reachable by the exact compile argv is a subset of the checked graph, including optional/default/target/workspace feature shapes, while no package code executes. (3) Add a pre-Cargo, manager-owned TOML/source closure walk over snapshot bytes. Before any cargo process, lexically and physically constrain workspace members, path dependencies, workspace inheritance, patches/replacements and all dependency tables to validated build_root bytes; reject absolute, escaping .., symlink/reparse and unresolved origins without opening an outside manifest. Then use Cargo output only as a consistency cross-check. Add adversarial relative/absolute/outside-marker cases proving external files are not read. (4) Specify canonical cross-platform TOML serialization for the manager-written operation-private Cargo config, including slash/backslash/quote/control/non-ASCII rules and canonical resolved vendor path; correct the false claim that no package-derived selection influences it. Extend the probe to execute the exact graph and compile argv with that exact config, a real vendored crates.io dependency, isolated CARGO_HOME/HOME/operator state, and byte-equivalent local plus external-repository source mappings. Preserve all six expected-red classifier controls and add controls for omitted --all-features, outside-root pre-read, config escaping and operator Cargo leakage. Re-run all task gates; accepted decisions 0007/0008 and frozen releases remain unchanged; macOS arm64 only remains the measured platform. Hand off revised decision/reference/results/fixtures/raw argv-env evidence for fresh independent review; no commit/stage/publish/pin.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-2e7daa, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-2e7daa)\nREWORK CYCLE 2 HANDOFF 2026-07-29: all four accepted review blockers closed, each by a host measurement, a contract change and an executable check; every cycle-1 green finding retained; decisions 0007/0008 and every frozen artifact untouched; macOS arm64 still the only measured platform; nothing staged, committed, published or pinned. (1) curator-rust-toolchain-v1 now has a closed MULTILINE normalization: 4096-byte and UTF-8/NUL gates, CRLF folded to LF so a Windows and a Unix probe agree, bare CR rejected, exactly one terminal LF not preceded by another, removed; V may carry interior LFs, C may not. Measured rustc -vV stdout is 192 bytes over 7 lines, so the old single-line rule provably rejected the toolchain the entry admits. Reproducible worked example published: V payload 191 bytes sha256 7d8e0833.., framed record 208 bytes sha256 7fc35c11..; C payload 35 bytes sha256 8d712854.., record 52 bytes sha256 d677e668... 13 vectors N1-N13, host-independent except N1. (2) The graph vector gains --all-features. Measured: without it an optional proc-macro dependency behind a non-default feature is ABSENT from packages[] entirely (feat,winonly vs feat,implicit,pm,winonly), so the old contract had a hole, not just a false sentence. The semantic is now stated exactly as the union over every platform, every dependency kind and every feature OF THE ROOT PACKAGE, measured NOT to be every feature of every package; the subset property is proved in four measured directions including that --locked does not start failing because Cargo.lock already records the reachable optional deps and cargo vendor has no --all-features flag. (3) New Stage P: a manager-owned closure over snapshot bytes with the manager own TOML parser, before any cargo process — manifest inventory including vendored manifests, forbidden-key gate, a closed seven-rule relative-path grammar decided ON THE DECLARED STRING BEFORE ANY FILESYSTEM CALL, dependency-origin and lock/vendor closure. Forced by two measurements: cargo metadata opens, parses and quotes an outside manifest during the graph phase; and an ancestor Cargo.toml carrying [workspace] plus [patch.crates-io] redirected a vendored dependency to an outside build-script package while workspace_members stayed length 1 and equal to the R package and resolve.root matched — the old G1 passes that shape. Ancestor Cargo.toml joins ancestor .cargo as a staging obligation; graph rows demoted to a cross-check plus new G0 (workspace_root == build root) and G11 (admitted-set agreement, a manager fault). package.build admitted only when exactly false, because cargo vendor normalization writes build = false. (4) The purity claim on the manager-written CARGO_HOME config is WITHDRAWN: build_root is package-selected. Containment is a closed representability rule plus a TOML literal string with no escape sequences plus a mandatory write-back re-parse; measured that an unescaped backslash in a basic string fails to load and that a naive writer emitted a file really carrying [net] offline = false and a [junk] table. The probe now runs the exact two argv over a vendored crates.io-source dependency with that exact config, isolated CARGO_HOME/HOME and 20 poisoned-PATH shims: graph 0, build 0, 0 PATH resolutions, artifact runs; both source-mode mappings over byte-identical build roots produce identical graphs with no outside file named. Separately on the host with a real cargo-vendored cfg-if 1.0.4 in a local root and in a cloned git repo: identical digests, identical graph after substitution, byte-identical executable. Probe green exit 0: 19/19 cases, P1/P2, 24 closure checks 0 verdicts, 10/10 controls failing as required (C7 omitted --all-features, C8 outside-root pre-read, C9 config injection, C10 operator Cargo leakage are new), 68 host-independent vectors 0 divergences, 13 structural checks 0 divergences; the absent-toolchain run still exits 0 and now still runs all 68 vectors. Policy object gains const feature_audit=root-all-features and source_closure=manager-prewalk-v1; three new diagnostics; conformance inventory 87 -> 134 vectors. NO NEW BOARD ELEMENT IS CREATED: the four fixes add implementation obligations to the already-linked TASK-260728-q283m8/13ioo0/2yxdo7/gjxj1v and schema obligations to TASK-260728-251p01, so creating elements would be decomposition for symmetry rather than for a requirement. Gates: probe gofmt/vet/build/test 0, probe runs 0, curator build/vet/test 0 and gofmt 0 files outside .temp; make check exit 2 and spec validate.py exit 1 are expected-red and fully attributed to other tasks scratch trees, with a clean-tree validate baseline at 0 and a scoped link check over the two authored documents at 0 broken of 4; golangci-lint NOT RUN, not installed on this host. Full evidence: TASK-260728-12pnm1_results.md and TASK-260728-12pnm1_rework-cycle-2-measurements.md.\nagent completed: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-2e7daa, pid=56673, exit=0)\nREVIEW CYCLE 2 DIRECTIVE: Independently review the Rust cycle-2 rework and replay its probe without editing producer artifacts. Verify the curator-rust-toolchain-v1 multiline normalization is total and cross-platform for UTF-8, CRLF/LF, bare CR, NUL, size and terminal-newline boundaries; recompute the published framed hashes. Challenge the --all-features model against the exact compile argv across root/dependency feature forwarding, optional/default/target/workspace/dependency-kind shapes and Cargo.lock/vendor behavior, proving every compilable package unit is contained in the checked graph. Audit Stage P as a true before-any-Cargo closure over snapshot bytes: all Cargo TOML dependency tables, workspace inheritance/members/excludes, patch/replace, vendored manifests, ancestor workspace/config, relative path grammar, symlink/reparse/unresolved origins and no outside read before rejection. Verify canonical operation-private Cargo config serialization and write-back parsing on POSIX and Windows-representable paths, isolated HOME/CARGO_HOME/PATH, exact graph/build argv, local/external byte equivalence and all ten expected-red controls. Re-run focused and applicable repository gates, distinguish unrelated dirty-tree failures, publish exact ACCEPTED or CHANGES REQUESTED evidence, and route accordingly. No artifact edits, staging, commit, publish or pin changes.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-efa5bc, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-efa5bc)

