notes:Execution base: branch independently from accepted curator-spec candidate /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-2kp3tv/curator-spec-worktree into a task-owned worktree; predecessor is read-only, and do not stage, commit, publish, advance pins, or claim native validation. This task runs in parallel with TASK-260728-1g0z69, which owns the detailed shared toolchain requirement/preflight/guidance wire contract. Avoid duplicating that contract: here decide and specify the versioned Rust/Swift/Kotlin local+external driver identities (six closed ids), artifact and launcher models, local source/build-root exclusions, skill-build.json target evolution, signing/platform boundaries, and prohibition on language detection/arbitrary package commands. Make any dependency on the toolchain contract explicit for downstream integration TASK-260728-251p01. Preserve frozen released artifacts and the current rc.5 candidate; provide normative decision/docs plus focused deterministic tests/gates appropriate to this boundary task.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-2249e1, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-2249e1)\nWorktree /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-2spy93/curator-spec-worktree created from accepted 2kp3tv candidate; verified byte-identical (diff -r --exclude=.git empty). Baseline gates green standalone: validate.py 0 (42 schemas / 422 files), python unittest 0 (29 tests), go test 0, go vet 0, gofmt clean. Predecessor worktree untouched.\nBoundary decision written as decisions/0008-additional-language-driver-boundary.md (drafted 0007, renumbered after TASK-260728-1g0z69 was found holding decisions/0007 in its own worktree). Fixes rc.6 version slots (manifest 8, descriptor 2, receipt 3 local / 4 external, marker 4, claim 4), six closed reserved identities (rust/swift/kotlin-native local+repository), one admitted artifact class native-executable-v1 with runtime-bundle rejected, unchanged context-excluded local build_roots and 3-member descriptor targets, explicit non-duplicating dependency on the TASK-260728-1g0z69 toolchain contract, and manager-worker-v1 retained with a generically restated graph so every go-v1/go-repository-v1 identity is byte-unchanged. Deliberately not re-versioned: Skillfile.dev.json, execution policy, native-control inventory, capability-evidence record, curator-build-source-v1. Code: tools/validate.py validate_additional_driver_boundary() (+216) and 15 new tests in tools/test_validate.py (29 -> 44). Exactly three files changed; nothing under conformance/, schemas/, release/, protocol/, profiles/. Gates green standalone in the task worktree: validate.py 0 (42 schemas / 422 files), unittest 0 (44 tests), go test 0, go vet 0, gofmt 0, compileall 0, git diff --check 0. Clean-checkout probe: make validate 0, make regenerate-check 0 twice, make release-check VERSION=1.0.0-rc.5 0. rc.5 candidate preserved: independently recomputed manifest digest sha256:9ba9b8ec... unchanged, regeneration byte-identical twice. Four negative probes proved the absence guard, the driver-const guard, the prose-surface guard and the bundle-member guard each reject. Honest limitation: the reserved-schema-slot guard is unreachable via the CLI because validate_schemas rejects an uncased schema first; it is exercised directly by a unit test. Nothing staged, committed, published, pinned, or claimed; no platform or native validation claim made.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-2249e1, pid=10232, exit=0)\nReviewer focus: independently challenge the architecture, not only validator gates. Verify the six IDs are closed and reservation is not admission; native-executable-only artifact/launcher model is coherent for Rust, Swift and Kotlin Native; local source-root rules and external skill-build.json schema evolution remain package-command-free; signing/platform/hardened claims stay honest. Cross-check against parallel TASK-260728-1g0z69: decision 0008 says descriptor schema 2 changes exactly one thing and adds no member, while the toolchain contract expects next-schema manifest and potentially descriptor requirements. Flag any contradiction that would make TASK-260728-251p01 impossible or force undocumented schema evolution. Check whether generalizing manager-worker-v1 process/session semantics is truly semantic preservation or needs v2; whether receipt 3/4 by source mode is unambiguous; all schemas 1-7 and rc.5 bytes must remain unchanged. Re-run focused guards, negative probes, deterministic/release gates; do not stage, commit, publish, pin, or claim native platforms.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-49e194, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-49e194)\nReview logbook 2026-07-28 — CHANGES REQUESTED and routed to analysis. Independent validation is green: 42 schemas / 422 vectors, 44 Python tests, 15 focused boundary tests, Go tests/vet/format, diff check, clean deterministic regeneration, and rc.5 release gate. Blocking contract defects remain: decision 0008 excludes the required manifest and optional descriptor toolchain requirement from the exact next-schema shapes; it widens the frozen Go-specific manager-worker-v1 identity into a generic policy without versioning; it says six identifiers are both admitted and merely reserved; and its validator false-accepts optional language, arbitrary command, and runtime_files fields. Exact evidence and re-review gate: TASK-260728-2spy93_review-verdict.md. No code, staging, commit, publication, pin, or platform claim changed by reviewer.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-49e194, pid=24978, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-fc2e6b, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-fc2e6b)\nRework cycle 1 started. Four blocking review findings accepted: (1) no legal wire location for the decision-0007 toolchain object in schema 8 / descriptor 2; (2) manager-worker-v1 semantically widened while claimed unchanged; (3) admitted-versus-reserved contradiction in section 2; (4) boundary gate uses deny-lists and false-accepts optional language on buildCommandV6, arbitrary command on skillBuildTargetV1, and runtime_files on buildRecordV2. Plan: reconcile decision 0008 with decision 0007 placement contract (named closed definitions buildCommandV8, repositoryBuildCommandV2, skillBuildTargetV2); mint manager-worker-v2 as a concurrent sibling policy for the six reserved drivers only, leaving manager-worker-v1 frozen and Go-only so no Go cache key or rc.5 byte moves; reserve capability-evidence-v2; split section 2 into an admitted wire set and a closed reserved namespace; replace the gate deny-lists with closed exact member-set tables plus reserved shapes; add negative coverage for the three demonstrated false accepts.\nRework 01 complete and ready for review. All four blocking findings addressed in decisions/0008-additional-language-driver-boundary.md (now 912 lines) plus tools/validate.py and tools/test_validate.py; still exactly three files different from the accepted TASK-260728-2kp3tv base. (1) Toolchain placement reconciled with decision 0007: reserved definitions buildCommandV8 and repositoryBuildCommandV2 carry a REQUIRED closed toolchain-requirement-v1 member, skillBuildTargetV2 carries it OPTIONAL, and buildCommandV6/repositoryBuildCommandV1/skillBuildTargetV1 are frozen and may never gain it; section 8 records why the REQUIRED member changes no go-v1 identity (the requirement is a gate, not a build input). (2) manager-worker-v1 left frozen and Go-only; manager-worker-v2 minted for the six reserved drivers as a concurrent sibling with an identical containment contract, an explicit non-ordering rule, and a closed driver-to-policy table made structural in claim schema 4. Knock-on capability-evidence-v2 reserved because v1 is closed to one policy and one record per operation while schema 8 admits mixed operations. The earlier claim that a new policy identity would invalidate rc.5 was false and is corrected. (3) Section 2 split into a named Admitted wire driver set (go-v1, go-repository-v1 only) and a named Reserved driver namespace (the six), with a single atomic transition owned by TASK-260728-251p01; both labels are gate-required terms. (4) Gate deny-lists replaced with closed exact member-set tables covering deployed, reserved and manager-authored driver-bearing definitions, plus a residual never-legal-name deny-list; all three demonstrated false accepts (optional language on buildCommandV6, arbitrary command on skillBuildTargetV1, runtime_files on buildRecordV2) now reject. Reserved-name absence scan extended to manager-worker-v2; capability-evidence-v2 deliberately excluded because that literal already appears in the frozen rc.5 corpus and release gate as the rejected example, so non-admission is proved positively instead, and the two literals TASK-260728-251p01 must move at rc.6 are named in the decision. Gates green standalone with the task venv: validate.py 0 (42 schemas / 422 files), unittest 0 (60 tests, was 44), go test 0, go vet 0, gofmt 0, compileall 0, git diff --check 0. Clean-checkout probe at commit 92cf7a5: make validate 0, make regenerate-check 0 twice, make release-check VERSION=1.0.0-rc.5 0. rc.5 preserved: manifest digest sha256:9ba9b8ecf6f06cafda1425aed3539dee8d12af43dabd36f803f4f420dbb1dacf unchanged, release/1.0.0-rc.5.json unchanged, two regenerations byte-identical. CLI plant-and-revert probes confirmed rejection of manager-worker-v2 on protocol/core.md and of toolchain added to the frozen skillBuildTargetV1, both files restored byte-identical. Nothing staged, committed, published, pinned, or claimed; no platform or native validation claim. Housekeeping: a stray .venv left inside the worktree by the previous cycle was removed. Board artifact note: TASK-260728-2spy93_decision-0008-... is the current decision; the older TASK-260728-2spy93_decision-0007-... attachment is a stale pre-renumber duplicate of the same file and could not be deleted because task-board resource delete aborts on an unrelated board element carrying an unparseable status value todo.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-fc2e6b, pid=31330, exit=0)\nREVIEW CYCLE 2 directive 2026-07-28: independently verify all four prior blocking findings against the final rework. Confirm schema-8 local and repository commands carry REQUIRED toolchain and descriptor-v2 target carries OPTIONAL toolchain while every frozen v1/v6/v7 shape stays exact; manager-worker-v1 remains Go-only and byte/semantic frozen, with manager-worker-v2 reserved only for the six new drivers and no Go cache-key change; capability-evidence-v2 reservation is coherent despite the rc.5 negative fixture already containing that rejected literal and remains unadmitted; admitted-wire and reserved-namespace sets are disjoint with one atomic transition; exact closed member-set validation rejects optional language, arbitrary command, runtime_files, generic selectors, install fields, and any unknown driver-bearing definition. Re-run all 60 tests, adversarial false-accept probes, deterministic regeneration and unchanged rc.5 release/digest gates. Treat stale decision-0007 attachment as superseded evidence only. Do not edit, stage, commit, publish, pin, or claim platforms; attach an explicit ACCEPTED or CHANGES REQUESTED verdict and route status.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-51258a, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-51258a)\nReview cycle 2 — CHANGES REQUESTED and routed to to-dev. All shipped gates are green (42 schemas, 422 vectors, 60 Python tests, Go tests/vet/format, deterministic regeneration twice, rc.5 release gate and unchanged manifest digest). Two blocking defects remain: the reserved shape validator accepts toolchain as an unconstrained string in buildCommandV8, repositoryBuildCommandV2 and skillBuildTargetV2; and claim schema 4 is required to admit all eight identifiers even though the decision permits rejected contracts to retire unused and tells integration to admit only accepted contracts. Exact evidence and re-review gate: TASK-260728-2spy93_review-verdict-cycle-2.md. No reviewer code, staging, commit, publication, pin, or platform claim.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-51258a, pid=47926, exit=0)\nREWORK CYCLE 2 directive 2026-07-28: continue in the existing task-owned curator-spec worktree and close only the two blockers in TASK-260728-2spy93_review-verdict-cycle-2.md. First, make the property schemas structural for buildCommandV8, repositoryBuildCommandV2 and skillBuildTargetV2: toolchain must be the exact closed toolchain-requirement-v1 schema/reference, not merely a field name; add adversarial red tests for string, open object, path-bearing object and wrong requirement reference in all three slots. Second, make claim-v4 driver assertions equal exactly the admitted set at minting, retaining per-driver policy consts; eight identifiers are allowed only conditionally if all six reserved contracts are accepted, while rejected/retired identifiers remain impossible to assert. Preserve all cycle-1 repairs, frozen v1/v6/v7 and manager-worker-v1 semantics, rc.5 bytes/digest, no staging/commit/publish/pin/platform claim. Rerun the full suite, deterministic regeneration twice and rc.5 release gate; attach a new rework artifact and hand off for another independent reviewer cycle.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-cf840f, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-cf840f)\nRework 02 complete and ready for review. Both cycle-2 blockers closed in the existing task worktree; still exactly three files different from the accepted TASK-260728-2kp3tv base (decision 0008 now 975 lines, tools/validate.py, tools/test_validate.py). (1) Toolchain placement is now structural, not nominal: decision 0008 allocates one shared definition toolchainRequirementV1, every slot property schema MUST be exactly {"$ref":"#/$defs/toolchainRequirementV1"} with no sibling keyword, and the definition MUST be exactly id + version with additionalProperties false. validate.py gains EXACT_PROPERTY_SCHEMAS, check_exact_property_schemas and check_toolchain_requirement_definition; a dangling reference fails, and a reserved shape minted without a driver (which would not be driver-bearing and would escape every table) fails. Decision 0007 names the object but fixes no $defs identifier, so naming it here is boundary placement ownership, not a redefinition; only the two members 0007 itself states are enforced and the version grammar stays 0007s. (2) Claim-v4 admission is now defined over the admitted set rather than a count: claim schema 4 admits exactly the admitted wire driver set as it stands when it is minted, eight identifiers if and only if all six reserved contracts are accepted, six if both Kotlin identifiers retire, and a retired identifier is structurally unassertable; per-driver execution_policy consts retained. check_claim_driver_admission plus the closed DRIVER_EXECUTION_POLICIES table enforce admitted-only assertions, per-driver policy pairing, closed four-member assertions without duplicates, and current-claim completeness, with older frozen claims allowed a subset. Sections 1, 4, 5, 8, 10, 11 and the security-impact section updated. Gates green standalone in the task worktree: validate.py 0 (42 schemas / 422 files), unittest 0 (71 tests, was 60), go test 0, go vet 0, gofmt 0, compileall 0, git diff --check 0. Clean-checkout probe at commit c12d0d8: make validate 0, make regenerate-check 0 twice, make release-check VERSION=1.0.0-rc.5 0. rc.5 preserved: manifest digest sha256:9ba9b8ecf6f06cafda1425aed3539dee8d12af43dabd36f803f4f420dbb1dacf and release/1.0.0-rc.5.json unchanged. Plant-and-revert CLI probes: buildCommandV8 with a string toolchain rejected with the exact-reference message, and an extra optional member on a claim-v3 driver assertion rejected by the claim gate; both files restored byte-identical and post-revert validate.py exit 0. Honest limitation: the reserved shapes and the requirement definition still do not exist on disk, so those checks are exercised by unit tests and plant-and-revert probes rather than by a shipped schema; the claim-v4 slot stays unminted, so the claim gate is proved against shipped claim v3 plus a synthetic newer sibling. Nothing staged, committed, published, pinned or claimed; no platform or native validation claim. Artifacts: TASK-260728-2spy93_rework-02.md (new) and the updated TASK-260728-2spy93_decision-0008-additional-language-driver-boundary.md.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-cf840f, pid=56648, exit=0)\nREVIEW CYCLE 3 directive 2026-07-28: independently verify both cycle-2 blockers are closed in the final rework. For buildCommandV8, repositoryBuildCommandV2 and skillBuildTargetV2, prove toolchain is exactly the sole $ref to #/$defs/toolchainRequirementV1 with no siblings, and that the referenced closed definition is exactly id+version/additionalProperties=false; challenge dangling refs, wrong refs, string/open/path-bearing objects, and a reserved shape lacking driver. For claim-v4, verify assertion membership equals exactly the admitted driver set at minting, every driver maps to its fixed execution policy, retired identifiers are structurally impossible, all-six acceptance yields eight while Kotlin retirement does not, and frozen older claims may remain subsets without widening current admission. Re-run all 71 tests, plant-and-revert adversarial probes, deterministic regeneration twice and unchanged rc.5 release/digest gates. No edits, staging, commit, publication, pin or platform claim; attach explicit verdict and route status.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-0a342c, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-0a342c)\nReview cycle