   258	### 2.3 The two version records and their normalization
   259	
   260	The `V` and `C` records are the only records with an empty path. Their payloads
   261	are the normalized stdout of `rustc -vV` and of `cargo --version` respectively.
   262	`rustc -vV` stdout is **multiline** — measured, 7 lines — so the normalization
   263	is defined over a multiline stream, and a single-line rule would reject the
   264	toolchain the entry admits.
   265	
   266	`normalize(stdout) -> payload`, in this order. Every failure is
   267	`build_toolchain_version_undetermined`; none of them has a default:
   268	
   269	1. `len(stdout) <= 4096` bytes.
   270	2. `stdout` is valid UTF-8.
   271	3. `stdout` contains no U+0000.
   272	4. Replace every CRLF (`0x0D 0x0A`) byte pair with a single LF (`0x0A`). This is
   273	   the only rewriting step, and it exists so that a Windows-hosted probe and a
   274	   Unix-hosted probe of the same distribution produce the same payload.
   275	5. After step 4 the stream contains no CR. A remaining CR — a bare `0x0D` — is a
   276	   rejection, not a line terminator.
   277	6. The stream is at least 2 bytes, its last byte is LF, and the byte before it
   278	   is not LF. That is the exact terminal-LF rule: exactly one terminator, and no
   279	   trailing blank line.
   280	7. Remove that final LF. The remainder is the `payload`.
   281	8. The `payload` is non-empty and contains no U+007F and no scalar below U+0020
   282	   other than LF.
   283	
   284	The `V` payload MAY contain interior LFs; that is the whole point of the rule.
   285	The `C` payload MUST additionally contain no LF at all: `cargo --version` is one
   286	line, and a multiline value there is `build_toolchain_version_undetermined`.
   287	
   288	Each record is appended with the framing of section 2.2, with `kind` the single
   289	ASCII byte `V` or `C` and an empty path:
   290	
   291	```text
   292	kind || uint64be(0) || uint64be(payload_byte_length) || payload
   293	```
   294	
   295	**Worked example, measured on this host.** Reproducible by anyone with the same
   296	distribution root; a different Rust release produces different bytes and
   297	different digests, which is the intended behaviour.
   298	
   299	| | `V` | `C` |
   300	|---|---|---|
   301	| raw stdout bytes | 192 | 36 |
   302	| payload bytes | 191 | 35 |
   303	| `sha256(payload)` | `7d8e08339e557ede5a9e565773c4cf17f83dea27f7d0c6591869f184bd1b81b5` | `8d712854de14f22840767bc824c5ac08098f35ddaa44437256e31b53cb546165` |
   304	| framed record bytes | 208 | 52 |
   305	| framed record header, hex | `56` `0000000000000000` `00000000000000bf` | `43` `0000000000000000` `0000000000000023` |
   306	| `sha256(framed record)` | `7fc35c11acae420849418f9c9f9b5681651beedc6d68f00bf1e4db022cd5f06b` | `d677e668d65108419fd197d147f31f2dda30a1364233440f3b0138d5185c2f78` |
   307	
   308	The `V` payload, verbatim, with `\n` written for the interior LF bytes:
   309	
   310	```text
   311	rustc 1.91.0 (f8297e351 2025-10-28)\nbinary: rustc\ncommit-hash: f8297e351a40c1439a467bbbb6879088047f50b3\ncommit-date: 2025-10-28\nhost: aarch64-apple-darwin\nrelease: 1.91.0\nLLVM version: 21.1.2
   312	```
   313	
   314	The `C` payload, verbatim:
   315	
   316	```text
   317	cargo 1.91.0 (ea2d97820 2025-10-10)
   318	```
   319	
   320	Because the whole verbose stream is bound rather than one extracted line, the
   321	identity changes when the commit hash, the commit date, the host line or the
   322	LLVM version changes, even if the release triple does not. That is stricter than
   323	binding `release: 1.91.0` alone, and it is the reason the multiline rule was
   324	taken rather than the single-line alternative.
   325	
   326	Conformance obligations for this rule, all host-independent except the first:
   327	
   328	| # | Vector | Required outcome |
   329	|---|---|---|
   330	| N1 | real `rustc -vV` stdout from the resolved root | normalizes, and both digests above reproduce |
   331	| N2 | the same content with every LF rewritten as CRLF | the **same** payload and the same digest |
   332	| N3 | the same content with one interior LF removed | normalizes, digest differs |
   333	| N4 | one payload byte changed | normalizes, digest differs |
   334	| N5 | two whole lines transposed | normalizes, digest differs |
   335	| N6 | a bare CR inserted | rejected |
   336	| N7 | no terminal LF | rejected |
   337	| N8 | two terminal LFs | rejected |
   338	| N9 | a NUL inserted | rejected |
   339	| N10 | invalid UTF-8 inserted | rejected |
   340	| N11 | empty stdout | rejected |
