   407	
   408	| Rejected when the manifest contains | Diagnostic |
   409	|---|---|
   410	| a top-level `cargo-features` key | `build_rust_manifest_key_forbidden` |
   411	| a `[workspace]` table, or `package.workspace` | `build_rust_workspace_forbidden` |
   412	| a `[patch]` or `[replace]` table | `build_rust_manifest_key_forbidden` |
   413	| any value equal to the inheritance form `{ workspace = true }` | `build_rust_manifest_key_forbidden` |
   414	| `package.build` whose value is anything other than the boolean `false` | `build_rust_build_script_forbidden` |
   415	| `package.links` | `build_rust_native_link_declaration_forbidden` |
   416	| `lib.proc-macro` or `lib.proc_macro` set to `true`, or `lib.plugin` set to `true` | `build_rust_proc_macro_forbidden` |
   417	| a `crate-type` or `crate_type` array with a member outside `{bin, lib, rlib}` | `build_rust_crate_type_forbidden` |
   418	| a dependency entry carrying `git`, `branch`, `tag`, `rev`, `registry` or `registry-index` | `build_rust_dependency_source_forbidden` |
   419	
   420	`package.build` is admitted only when it is exactly `false`. **Measured**: the
   421	`cargo vendor` normalization of `cfg-if 1.0.4` writes `build = false`
   422	explicitly, so a rule that rejected the mere presence of the key would reject
   423	ordinary vendored crates. The manifest inventory covers vendored manifests, so
   424	these rows also decide a vendored crate's build script and crate type before
   425	Cargo reads either.
   426	
   427	This gate over-rejects in one known direction: a `[patch]` table in a vendored
   428	manifest is inert to Cargo outside a workspace root, and Stage P rejects it
   429	anyway. That is deliberate — the rule is closed and needs no reasoning about
   430	which manifest Cargo will treat as the workspace root.
   431	
   432	### 4.3 The closed relative-path grammar
   433	
   434	A **path-bearing key** is any of:
   435	
   436	- `path` inside any entry of `dependencies`, `dev-dependencies`,
   437	  `build-dependencies`, or the same three tables under any `target.<cfg>` table;
   438	- `lib.path`, and `path` inside any entry of `bin`, `test`, `bench` or
   439	  `example`;
   440	- `package.readme` and `package.license-file` when their value is a string.
   441	
   442	Every path-bearing value `Vp` in every member of `M` MUST satisfy all of:
   443	
   444	1. `Vp` is a TOML string, valid UTF-8, non-empty, at most 1024 bytes;
   445	2. `Vp` contains no U+0000, no scalar below U+0020, and no U+007F;
   446	3. `Vp` contains no `\` — a Cargo manifest path uses `/` on every platform, and
   447	   a backslash is rejected rather than interpreted;
   448	4. `Vp` does not begin with `/`;
   449	5. `Vp` has no `<letter>:` drive prefix, no `//` UNC prefix, and no first
   450	   component equal to `~`;
   451	6. splitting `Vp` on `/`, no component is empty, `.` or `..`;
   452	7. no component ends with `.` or U+0020, and no component, case-folded and
   453	   truncated at its first `.`, is one of `CON PRN AUX NUL COM1`…`COM9`
   454	   `LPT1`…`LPT9`.
   455	
   456	Rules 4 through 6 make `D/Vp` — the lexical join with the directory of the
   457	containing manifest — provably a descendant of `D`, and `D` is a descendant of
   458	`R` by section 4.1, so the admitted path set is closed under `R` by
   459	construction. Rules 3, 5 and 7 exist so that the same snapshot is admitted or
   460	rejected identically on macOS and on Windows.
   461	
   462	A violation is `build_rust_input_outside_build_root`, and it is decided **on the
   463	declared string**, before any filesystem call is made with that string. The
   464	manager MUST NOT stat, open, canonicalize or resolve a value that has not passed
   465	rules 1 through 7.
   466	
   467	For a value that passes, the physical check is:
   468	
   469	- for a dependency `path`: the joined path MUST exist, MUST be a directory, and
   470	  MUST contain `Cargo.toml`; that manifest MUST already be a member of `M`;
   471	- for any other path-bearing key: if the joined path exists it MUST be a regular
   472	  file or directory; non-existence is not a Stage P failure, because a vendored
   473	  crate may declare a target whose sources were not vendored and no admitted
   474	  compile command builds it;
   475	- in both cases every component of the joined path, checked with a
   476	  non-following stat, MUST NOT be a symbolic link or a reparse point, and the
   477	  canonical form of the joined path MUST still have `R` as a path-component
   478	  prefix.
   479	
   480	A physical-check failure is `build_rust_input_outside_build_root`.
   481	
   482	### 4.4 Dependency origin closure
   483	
   484	After section 4.2 has removed `git`, `rev`, `branch`, `tag`, `registry` and
   485	`registry-index`, every dependency entry in every member of `M` has exactly one
   486	admitted origin:
   487	
   488	- a `path` value admitted by section 4.3, which resolves inside `R`; or
   489	- a plain registry dependency with no `registry` key, which the manager-written
   490	  source replacement of section 6.1 binds to `V` and to nothing else.
   491	
   492	Anything else is `build_rust_dependency_source_forbidden`.
   493	
   494	### 4.5 Lock and vendor closure
   495	
   496	`R/Cargo.lock` — and only that lock file; the nested `Cargo.lock` a vendored
   497	crate carries is not read — MUST parse, and every `[[package]]` entry MUST have
   498	either no `source` key or a `source` exactly equal to
