trols, 8/8 structural checks; Curator test/vet 0; resource/worktree documents byte-identical. Four contract blockers remain: curator-rust-toolchain-v1 rejects multiline rustc -vV under its own normalization; the fixed cargo metadata argv lacks --all-features while the contract and vector 19 claim an all-feature union; G6/G7 discover outside-root path dependencies only after Cargo has read/resolved them; and the probe does not exercise the exact manager-written Cargo config, vendored dependency, exact argv, or both source modes, while Windows TOML path serialization is unspecified. Rust-version classified narrowing and macOS closure/platform/signing boundaries otherwise pass review. Full evidence and re-review gate: TASK-260728-12pnm1_review-verdict-cycle-1.md. Reviewer supplied no commit_ack.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-de06b1, pid=21862, exit=0)\nREWORK CYCLE 2 DIRECTIVE (review cycle 1): Resolve exactly the four accepted review blockers in the preserved Rust task worktree; retain every green finding and do not widen platform claims. (1) Make curator-rust-toolchain-v1 independently computable from real multiline rustc -vV. Prefer a closed multiline normalization (CRLF to LF, reject bare CR/NUL/invalid UTF-8, exact terminal-LF rule) inside the existing length framing, or bind one explicitly extracted whole release line; whichever is chosen must update decision/reference/identity example/probe plus positive and line/byte mutation vectors. (2) Keep the deliberate conservative all-feature union and add --all-features to the exact metadata argv; prove every package unit reachable by the exact compile argv is a subset of the checked graph, including optional/default/target/workspace feature shapes, while no package code executes. (3) Add a pre-Cargo, manager-owned TOML/source closure walk over snapshot bytes. Before any cargo process, lexically and physically constrain workspace members, path dependen